{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 3109 (commit ae02e364465, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved).\n\nMeasured before the fix: a bounded ticket-create git commit takes about 0.025 s on this host, so the 1.0 s kill bound had large headroom on a healthy commit. A git shim that sleeps 1.3 s before commit, with no repack involved, reproduces exactly the reported 'git timed out after 1.0s'. So the old test failed on any slow commit, whatever the cause.\n\nThe test now sets GIT_TRACE2_EVENT and asserts the structural invariant instead: with the _AUTOMAINT_OFF suppression in place, no maintenance, gc, repack, pack-objects or multi-pack-index process is a descendant of a git commit process. The 1.0 s _GIT_TIMEOUT patch is gone and production keeps its 30 s default. A detector test empties _AUTOMAINT_OFF and must find 'maintenance run --auto' under the commit.\n\nScratch checks: the invariant test fails with _AUTOMAINT_OFF emptied, and passes with every git commit delayed 1.3 s.\n\nUnverified: the original failing run had no trace, so the exact slow step in that run is unknown. The fix removes the dependence on wall-clock time; it does not identify what stalled that commit."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792941472443157001,"uuid":"e8061e63-02bd-42f6-919b-f156d14f1f99"}